      "schema:description": "`THCP` is the owner's term, registered as a search string on 2026-11-11 by owner direction (ISS-20261111-TAX-040). On 2026-11-11 the owner confirmed the intended meaning of the registered term: the tetrahydrocannabiphorol C7 homologue family, with the Δ8/Δ9 positional isomer UNSPECIFIED (ISS-20261111-TAX-040 addendum). This fixes the search-topic family only. Δ8-THCP and Δ9-THCP are separate substances, the registered string identifies neither isomer, and no Google Trends or YouTube result is attributed to an isomer. No single external record denotes the family, so this concept carries no skos:exactMatch and no CAS number, PubChem CID, UNII, ChEBI ID or Wikidata QID: the per-isomer records are documented in docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md as evidence about the isomers, never as this concept's identifier. The single-substance chemical identity remains UNCONFIRMED and the term stays in compound_identity_unverified, an administrative registration-state category, so this placement asserts no route/origin, natural occurrence, chemical class, synonym or regulatory status; the family scope recorded here is the term's documented scope, not a chemical-class link. The published chemistry is recorded in the ledger with its limits: Citti et al. 2019 (DOI 10.1038/s41598-019-56785-1) reports Δ9-THCP as a C7 homologue, and the frequently repeated 33-fold figure is a CB1 binding-affinity ratio, not human potency. ISS-20261015-TAX-027 recorded a decision not to register this term because no name, route placement or identifier evidence existed; the owner's 2026-11-11 scope decision supersedes that decision for this term (ISS-20261111-TAX-040). The COA panel entry records THCP as not detected in one sample, which is an observation about that sample, not a placement basis. **Query limitation:** Google Trends and YouTube series for `THCP` / `THCP リキッド` measure occurrences of those literal strings; `THCP` is an acronym that can match unrelated text, and a matching result is not evidence of tetrahydrocannabiphorol content. Evidence that would move the term out of this category: a documented single chemical name with a verified external identifier, or a recorded source naming the single substance and its route/origin; the basis belongs in docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md.",
      "schema:termCode": "compound_thcp"
    },
