      "@type": "schema:DefinedTerm",
      "@id": "https://japan-cannabinoid-trends.routeflags.com/taxonomy/compound_thcjd",
      "schema:name": "THCJD",
      "schema:inDefinedTermSet": {
        "@type": "schema:DefinedTermSet",
        "@id": "https://japan-cannabinoid-trends.routeflags.com/taxonomy/compound-thcjd-scheme"
      },
      "schema:description": "`THCJD` is the owner's term, registered as a search string on 2026-11-11 by owner direction (ISS-20261111-TAX-040). On 2026-11-11 the owner confirmed the intended meaning of the registered term: the THC-JD / 3-octyl-THC C8 homologue family, with the Δ8/Δ9 positional isomer UNSPECIFIED (ISS-20261111-TAX-040 addendum). This fixes the search-topic family only. The spelling `THCJD` (no hyphen) is the owner's search string, not an authoritative registry name; the naming and the Δ8/Δ9 3-octyl-THC identification are recorded in Tanaka & Kikura-Hanajiri 2024 (DOI 10.1248/yakushi.24-00029). The Δ8 and Δ9 3-octyl-THC forms are separate substances, the registered string identifies neither isomer, and no Google Trends or YouTube result is attributed to an isomer. No single external record denotes the family, so this concept carries no skos:exactMatch and no CAS number, PubChem CID, UNII, ChEBI ID or Wikidata QID: the per-isomer records are documented in docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md as evidence about the isomers, never as this concept's identifier. The single-substance chemical identity remains UNCONFIRMED and the term stays in compound_identity_unverified, an administrative registration-state category, so this placement asserts no route/origin, natural occurrence, chemical class, synonym or regulatory status; the family scope recorded here is the term's documented scope, not a chemical-class link. Regulatory status is not claimed: no regulatory source was evaluated for this change, so the family confirmation neither sets nor implies one. Commercial products sold under this kind of label have shown severe label/content mismatches (Munger et al. 2026, DOI 10.26828/cannabis/2026/000348), and the 19-fold potency figure circulating in that market is an industry claim, not a measured human potency. **Query limitation:** Google Trends and YouTube series for `THCJD` / `THCJD リキッド` measure occurrences of those literal strings; `THCJD` is an acronym that can match unrelated text, and a matching result is not evidence of 3-octyl-THC content. Evidence that would move the term out of this category: a documented single chemical name with a verified external identifier, or a recorded source naming the single substance and its route/origin; the basis belongs in docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md.",
      "schema:termCode": "compound_thcjd"
    },
    {
      "@type": "schema:DefinedTerm",
      "@id": "https://japan-cannabinoid-trends.routeflags.com/taxonomy/compound_thcpo",
      "schema:name": "THCPO",
      "schema:inDefinedTermSet": {
        "@type": "schema:DefinedTermSet",
        "@id": "https://japan-cannabinoid-trends.routeflags.com/taxonomy/compound-thcpo-scheme"
