      "schema:alternateName": [
        "カンナビシクロール (CBL)",
        "CBL"
      ],
      "schema:description": "`CBL` is the owner's term for **cannabicyclol**, confirmed by the owner on 2026-11-11. Identity and identifiers were verified against Wikidata Q907909 (en label 'cannabicyclol', CAS 21366-63-2, PubChem CID 30607, formula C21H30O2), the FDA GSRS record for UNII MP5WZK8M5U (substanceClass chemical, definitionLevel COMPLETE; names CANNABICYCLOL / CANNABIPINOL / PENTYLCANNABICYCLOL; CAS 21366-63-2, PubChem CID 59444380, formula C21H30O2) and PubChem CID 59444380 ('Cannabicyclol', stereospecified). PubChem CID 30607 is the stereo-unspecified / (+/-) record and carries CAS 67920-00-7 as a synonym, so the two CAS numbers circulate with different stereochemistry; this concept asserts no single CAS number as its identifier. The owner's query strings `CBL` and `CBL リキッド` are unchanged. The 2025 study of CBL describes it as a minor phytocannabinoid and reports acid-catalysed conversion of cannabichromene (CBC) to CBL, with the structure confirmed by X-ray crystallography (Haghdoost et al. 2025, J Nat Prod, DOI 10.1021/acs.jnatprod.4c00977, PMID 39811943); cannabicyclol has also been quantified among phytocannabinoids in cannabis material (PMID 33839545). Those detections do not establish enzymatic biosynthesis or occurrence in the intact living plant, and no biosynthetic route is asserted here. Placement in compound-minor therefore records only 'a phytocannabinoid other than the major pair'. The ja label follows the Japanese rendering used in Japanese-language scientific reporting (Wikidata's ja label is different); no chemical-class link is asserted because the chemical-class taxonomy has no CBL-type class, and no regulatory status is claimed. **Query limitation:** Google Trends and YouTube series for `CBL` measure occurrences of that literal string, not verified cannabicyclol content, and `CBL` is a short acronym that can match unrelated text. The existing samples are string-match observations, not proof of content relevance. Basis and source record: docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md (ISS-20261111-TAX-040 addendum).",
      "schema:termCode": "compound_cbl"
    },
