      "schema:description": "`Δ8-THCA` is the owner's search term, registered on 2026-11-11 (ISS-20261111-TAX-041) as one of three distinct search-topic concepts that replace the generic chemical interpretation of `THCA`; `compound_thca` remains the separate registration of the literal string `THCA`. The term is registered as a search string, not as a substance identification. The single-substance chemical identity remains UNCONFIRMED. This change did not verify a structural or registry source for `Δ8-THCA`: the sources cited for the other two THCA topics document the Δ9 series only, where THCA-A (2-carboxy-THC) and THCA-B (4-carboxy-THC) are distinct isomers (Moreno-Sanz 2016, DOI 10.1089/can.2016.0008; Filer 2021, DOI 10.1089/can.2021.0003, PMCID PMC8612408). The registered term names a Δ8 series but does not state the A or B carboxyl arrangement, so it does not establish a single structure; no identifier is inferred from the Δ9 nomenclature. This concept carries no skos:exactMatch and no CAS number, PubChem CID, UNII, ChEBI ID or Wikidata QID: this change did not verify or select a single external record for the registered string, and the owner's confirmation fixes the query topic, not result-level substance identity. It stays in compound_identity_unverified, an administrative registration-state category, so the placement asserts no route/origin, natural occurrence, chemical class, structure, synonym or regulatory status. No skos:related link to compound_thca, compound_thc, the neutral Δ8-THC compound (which has no taxonomy concept) or another new concept is asserted. **Query limitation:** Google Trends and YouTube series for `Δ8-THCA` / `Δ8-THCA リキッド` measure occurrences of those literal strings; a matching result is not evidence of Δ8-THCA content. Evidence that would move the term out of this category: a documented structural or nomenclatural source that fixes the Δ8 acid's carboxyl arrangement, together with a verified external identifier; the basis belongs in docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md.",
