      "schema:description": "`Δ9-THCH` is the owner's search term, registered on 2026-11-15 (ISS-20261115-TAX-045) as one of the 27 forms the owner enumerated for registration from the study's candidate-form inventory in `datasets/cannabinoid-raw-collection`. The term is a registered search string, not a substance identification: the single-substance chemical identity remains UNCONFIRMED. The evidence recorded for this form in the study inventory is a statutory structural group: Consumer Affairs Agency material on THCH as a designated substance records Δ8-THCH and Δ9-THCH as covered (individual designation 2023-08-04, generic designation 2023-09-10) (research/regulatory-status/THCH.md §1). No registry record was selected and product analytical identification was not confirmed in this repository. A statutory structural listing is a legal structural fact, not a product detection and not a claim about any result. No identifier property and no `skos:exactMatch` are assigned to this taxonomy concept: any CAS / PubChem / UNII / ChEBI / Wikidata / IUPAC values quoted in this note are recorded evidence in `docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md`, were not re-verified in this change, and were not selected for the registered query. It stays in compound_identity_unverified, an administrative registration-state category, so this placement asserts no route/origin, natural occurrence, chemical class, structure, synonym, pharmacology, safety or regulatory status, and it asserts no relation to the inventory parent term `THCH`: that grouping in the candidate table organised the rows and is not a structural or synonym claim. **Query limitation:** Google Trends and YouTube series for `Δ9-THCH` / `Δ9-THCH リキッド` measure occurrences of those literal strings; a matching result is not evidence of the Δ9 form content. Evidence that would move the term out of this category: a verified external record selected for the registered string, or a recorded product identification for this form; the basis belongs in docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md.",
      "schema:termCode": "compound_delta9_thch"
